  "decision_conditions": [
    "The\r\nintroduction of an additional residential dwelling is unacceptable in principle\r\nas the required bulk refuse and recycling bins would exceed 15m to the public\r\nhighway. Therefore, the local authority would be unable to perform their statutory\r\nduty of waste collection for domestic households failing to comply with Policy\r\n57 (Amenity) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).",
    "The\r\nproposed extension, by reason of its design, position and bulk, would be an unduly\r\ndominant and bulky addition which is out of keeping with the character of the host\r\nbuilding to the visual detriment of the wider area contrary to Policy 53 (Delivering\r\nHigh Quality Design) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).",
    "The\r\nproposal incorporates inadequate means of pedestrian access to the site whereby\r\nthe access road is insufficiently lit and easily permeated, contrary to Policy 53 (Delivering\r\nHigh Quality Design) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).",
    "In\r\nthe absence of a Tree Survey (in line with British Standard 5837:2012 Trees in\r\nRelation to Design, Demolition and Construction), to identify the impact of the\r\ndevelopment on the existing trees, along with the required protection and\r\nmitigation measures, a full assessment of the acceptability of the development\r\nand assurance of the protection of local biodiversity could not be carried out,\r\nand therefore it cannot be confirmed that the development would be in\r\ncompliance with ﻿Policy 80 of the\r\nWaltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).",
    "In\r\nthe absence of a satisfactory Outline Construction Logistic Plan, a full\r\nassessment&nbsp;of how the proposed development would be built or serviced\r\nwithout severely affecting the public highway could not be made in line with\r\nPolicies T7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 65 of the Waltham Forest Local\r\nPlan LP1 (2024).",
    "The\r\napplicant failed to enter into a s106 agreement and therefore not in compliance\r\nwith Policy 94 (Infrastructure and Developer Contributions) of the Waltham\r\nForest Local Plan LP1 (2024)&nbsp;(figures applicable at the time of the\r\nassessment of the application):Car\r\nFree Development - the development is to be classified as car-free and\r\nresidents will not be eligible for parking permits.A\r\ncondition survey of the of the adjoining carriageway and footway on Grange Park\r\nRoad, as well as any major junctions along the route to the site proposed in\r\nthe CLP showing the where the photos were taken on the public highway.Financial\r\ncontribution of £627.00 is requested towards the Epping Forest SAMMFinancial\r\ncontribution of £250 is requested toward CLP monitoring.Financial\r\ncontribution of £1,000 is requested toward improving walking and cycling\r\nfacilities within the sites vicinity which will directly benefit future\r\nresidents of the site.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFinancial\r\ncontribution of 5% for s106 monitoring fees."
  ],
